# Input
```yaml
# should generate diagnostics
person:
  name: John Doe
  age: 50
  name: Jane Doe

person2: { name: John, age: 50, name: Jane }

person3:
  name: John Doe
  "name": Jane Doe
  'name': Baby Doe

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid.yaml:3:3 lint/nursery/noDuplicateMapKeys ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  × The key name was already declared.
  
    1 │ # should generate diagnostics
    2 │ person:
  > 3 │   name: John Doe
      │   ^^^^
    4 │   age: 50
    5 │   name: Jane Doe
  
  i This is where a duplicated key was declared again.
  
    3 │   name: John Doe
    4 │   age: 50
  > 5 │   name: Jane Doe
      │   ^^^^
    6 │ 
    7 │ person2: { name: John, age: 50, name: Jane }
  
  i If a key is defined multiple times, only the last definition takes effect. Previous definitions are ignored.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

```

